From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -banks, -bank_columns, -bank_order
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-banks splits the words into banks, contiguous or interleaved in the
address (-bank_order), -bank_columns of them side by side and the rest
stacked, for an array's aspect ratio and for the bank counts register
files use (XiangShan's 224 words in 4 interleaved banks). With banks
every port decodes every word's whole address, an AND2 tree per word,
so a bank need not be a power of two words and any placement of words
reads and writes alike; a row holds -bank_columns words, laid out as the
column mux lays out its words. A read port is one tristate bitline
shared by every word, or one AND-OR tree over all of them. Without
-banks, nothing changes. Not with -column_mux_ratio above 1 or
-use_latch.

Also: an array with fewer rows than address bits got no address
inverters (ports_per_col was 0), so its decoders read floating
literals; at least one port's inverters now go in each column.

Tested: src/ram/test/banks_asap7.tcl.

Commit 5 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
